# Observability

If a trade goes wrong, we must be able to determine why.

---

## Structured Logs

Every trading event should include stable identifiers where available:

- event_id
- timestamp
- market_id
- strategy_id
- order_id
- client_order_id
- position_id

---

## Metrics

Track at minimum:

Market:
- markets observed
- signals generated
- stale-data events

Execution:
- orders submitted
- orders acknowledged
- orders rejected
- fills
- partial fills
- cancellations
- fill rate
- execution latency

Risk:
- approvals
- rejections by reason
- exposure
- daily loss
- position limits

Trading:
- realized P&L
- unrealized P&L
- fees
- average entry
- average exit
- slippage
- win rate
- drawdown

---

## Slippage

Always distinguish:

expected price
from
actual execution price.

Never report theoretical P&L as realized P&L.

---

## Audit Trail

Trading decisions must be traceable from:

signal
→ risk decision
→ order
→ fill
→ position
→ exit
→ settlement
→ P&L
